<%#
  Rendered into the session card by the dashboard.

  The binding here is the BatchConnect::Session, so user_context is available --
  the launch form values, read back from user_defined_context.json. That is a
  different binding from view.html.erb, which is why the editor choice has to
  reach the Connect button through the pod's Secret instead of from here.

  Keys are form attribute ids, so this tracks form.yml's `editor` and
  `login_shell`. Both are shown because both change what the session is, and
  nothing else on the card reveals either -- the dashboard shows host, times and
  session id, and the app title is fixed by manifest.yml.
-%>
<%- editor = user_context["editor"].to_s -%>
<%- shell  = user_context["login_shell"].to_s -%>
**Editor:** <%= editor == "code" ? "VS Code" : "JupyterLab" %>
<%- unless shell.empty? -%>
 &middot; **Shell:** `<%= File.basename(shell) %>`
<%- end -%>

Run `cirrus-check` in a terminal to confirm cluster access.
